---559023410-851401618-1056120100=:19985
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII

This patch adds a broadcast tracking module (ip_conntrack_module). It is
not finished yet (one minor remaining problem) but i would like to know if
this is viewed as beeing useful. It is able to track outgoing (local)
broadcast  and incoming broadcast (anycast). It works by registering an
expectation for the replies and re-registering them for the not-anycast
case when it is confirmed. The problem mentioned before is that each
re-registration refreshes the timeout, but it's easy solvable by letting
the helper set the timeout itself. The patch expects a kernel with all
pending patches applied. A version for vanilla-kernels is available at
http://trash.net/~kaber/ip_conntrack_broadcast .

Best regards,
Patrick

